<title>DUBAI: Saudi Aramco cuts bunker fuel prices.</title>
<headline>Saudi Aramco cuts bunker fuel prices.</headline>
<dateline>DUBAI 1997-07-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Saudi Aramco has cut its A-960 bunker fuel by $1 a tonne to $102 ($15.66 a barrel) from Ras Tanura and Dammam and $93 ($14.27) from Jeddah and Yanbu.</p>
<p>A-888 bunker diesel is left unchanged at $199 a tonne from Gulf ports and $180 from Red Sea ports, Aramco said.</p>
<p>Prices are effective July 3.</p>
</text>
